### ShopSphere - hand-run requests (IntelliJ HTTP client / VS Code REST Client). Everything goes through the gateway.
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Log in as the demo customer (dev seed). The token is stored for the following requests.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&username=alice&password=Alice#Pass123

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
@refresh = {{login.response.body.$.refresh_token}}

### Public catalogue: filters, sorting, pagination (v2)
GET {{host}}/api/v2/products?q=laptop&category=electronics&sort=price,asc&page=0&size=5

### Legacy v1 (look at the Deprecation / Sunset / Link response headers)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?category=books

### Place an order. Re-sending with the same Idempotency-Key returns the original order (200) instead of a new one.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: 6f1d2c1e-8f5b-4d0e-9a52-0c3b1e8f7a01
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productId": "PUT-A-REAL-PRODUCT-ID-HERE", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### My orders
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Notifications created asynchronously from Kafka order events
GET {{host}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rotate the refresh token (the old one becomes invalid)
POST {{host}}/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={{refresh}}

### OIDC discovery + public signing keys
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

###
GET {{host}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### Who am I (claims of my token)
GET {{host}}/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
